{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Hod</b> — Although His deeds are great, they require those who seek them and are made plain, for the work of HaShem is visible to the eye; therefore, hod and hadar." "And the meaning of <b>ve-tzidkato</b> — all His doing is tzedek."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 111, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:39:22.563057119Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}